      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To address suburban and rural concerns, the report should highlight a phased approach where federal grants fund regional rail connectivity and rural highway upgrades simultaneously rather than choosing one over the other. Acknowledging that highways provide necessary flexibility for dispersed rural economies can build trust, while data showing highway expansion often kills neighborhoods due to missing middle housing and traffic bottlenecks counters the long-term mobility argument. Finally, emphasizing that investment is purpose-driven—prioritizing rapid rail for transit corridors and targeted grants for rural road maintenance—ensures equitable outcomes across all jurisdictions.",
